"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-11.md"}],"metadata":{"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2007-11"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"After Korean Eastern Presbytery tried, convicted, deposed, and excommunicated TE Eliot Lee, the SJC sustained his appeal and reversed the disposition and excommunication. The decisive reason was procedural: the record did not show timely service of the indictment/citations or the required 14-day trial notice, violating BCO 32-3, 32-7, and 32-10. Under BCO 42-9, the SJC rendered the decision it thought should have been made, finding no strong presumption of guilt under BCO 31-2 justified formal process; it added pastoral counsel, expressly not censure."}},{"id":"bco:22-6--case:cases/ga38_2010__stub_2009-16.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga38_2010__stub_2009-16.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Eliot Lee v. Korean Eastern","year":2009,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga38_2010__stub_2009-16.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga38_2010__stub_2009-16.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-6--case:cases/ga38_2010__stub_2009-16.md:occ-55d0d6a498e0","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga38_2010__stub_2009-16.html","repository_path":"cases/ga38_2010__stub_2009-16.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga38_2010__stub_2009-16.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["ecclesiastical polity","interim pastor status","stated supply pastors","presbytery authority","civil court jurisdiction","congregational consent","PCA non-hierarchical nature"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2009-16"],"body":"SJC","synopsi