/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.html","repository_path":"cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":155},"excerpt":"…of the term of its interim pastor [TE Lee], has acted in accord with BCO 22-6, i.e. stated supply relationships may not exceed one (1) year, but can be renewed at the request of the Session; so that HKPC's Session's actions show that it understood…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.md"},{"id":"bco:22-6--case:cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.md:occ-1e9672d78081","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.html","repository_path":"cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":166},"excerpt":"(with a term of one (1) year), pursuant to BCO 22-6. KEP tacitly held","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["stated supply","interim pastor","pastoral relationship","judicial commission"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2007-7"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Lee challenged Korean Eastern Presbytery’s actions affecting his interim pastoral relationship, alleging that its October 3, 2006 meeting lacked a quorum. The SJC held the complaint moot and declared every action taken at that meeting null and void—not merely those concerning his church. The meeting opened with only two ruling elders when three were required, and the minutes did not establish when a quorum was later achieved; its presence therefore could not be presumed."}},{"id":"bco:22-6--case:cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Antioch Session v. Eastern Carolina Presbytery","year":1994,"disposition":"not_sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-6--case:cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.md:occ-97836142c53f","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1992-09a.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["licensure","creation","age of earth","flood (local vs. universal)","divorce and remarriage","church office qualifications","stated supply","system of doctrine","theonomy","presbytery jurisdiction over membership"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1992-9a"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Antioch Session challenged Peterson’s licensure based on his prior divorce, creation and local-flood views, reversal of a committee recommendation, and close vote; it also challenged his regular preaching before licensure. The SJC rejected the licensure specifications because Presbytery had thoroughly examined repentance and doctrinal adherence, and no definitive PCA standard required exclusion on these facts. It sustained the pre-licensure supply issue under BCO 19-1, 22-5, and 22-6 and enjoined greater future circumspection. The licensure remained undisturbed; the ruling was expressly case-specific."}},{"id":"bco:22-6--overture:ga37_2009:4","record_id":"overture:ga37_2009:4","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 22-5 and 22-6 to Add 'Interim Pastor'","year":2009,"disposition":